  177:         "problem": "Current exported DataRootLease value contains mutex, file and borrowed flag directly. External code can copy the value without touching private fields. Revision03 explicitly protects borrow copies but does not explicitly protect parent copies or distinguish old ReturnBorrow from the new maintenance borrower. A copied parent could Close its copied state while a maintenance borrower is active; a reused boolean could let ReturnBorrow clear the wrong borrow.",
  178:         "required": "Make every DataRootLease value point to one private heap owner-state containing mutex, file, generation, closed state and active borrow identity/kind. Copies, Root/Held/Close, old Borrow/ReturnBorrow and new Maintenance methods must consult that same state. Nil/zero parent and borrow must fail closed without panic. Legacy ReturnBorrow may release only an active legacy coordinator borrow; it must reject an active maintenance borrow. Maintenance Release consumes only its exact private generation-bound token, and cannot release a later or legacy borrow. Parent Close refuses either live borrow and invalidates all copies atomically on successful close. No lock held while recursively calling a method that takes it.",
