  197:           "internal/domain/backup_queue_upgrade.go:320-337",
  198:           "19.stdout.raw"
  199:         ],
  200:         "problem": "All five plans enter the new adapter, but queue/configuration branches call upgradePaths again and then open templates/source later. Merely retaining coordinator.lock and checking a path at adapter entry does not stop a source/root rename or alias change before a downstream open. The text requires revalidation after normalization but does not place it in these existing common call sites.",
  201:         "required": "Within the existing allowed backup_upgrade.go, make the shared upgradePaths path finish by validating opt.sourceLease against the final normalized root/source for guarded production workflows, before returning to any branch. The private adapter/source borrow must retain native no-delete/rename guards for the exact root path components and source file identity until all downstream DB defers complete; metadata handles may share read/write needed by SQLite but cannot permit identity replacement. Check canonical containment, no reparse and exact native file identities. Existing prepared wrapper Check remains required. Public UpgradeLocal/UpgradePreparedAbandonmentBackup stay fail-closed before any provider/key/template/store work. Isolated private legacy algorithm fixtures cannot count as guarded entry proof. This selected central implementation avoids adding queue/configuration production files; if the builder cannot implement these persistent guards, STOP and request an exact scope addition for explicit checks, rather than omit the invariant.",
