  228:         "problem": "Replacement can die after ReplaceFile while journal remains PUBLISHING and target already equals NewBytes. Applying ordinary history-current/latest-terminal-target comparison before granting its exact own inspection permit would reject this legitimate recovery. Treating the permit as a broad pending exemption would create the opposite flaw.",
  229:         "required": "Freeze two separate pure predicates in the shared reader: ordinary acquisition validates complete history and current terminal target; exact-own inspection validates the full causal history including the one exact pending operation and its permitted current old/new state using the existing replacementRecover applied/unapplied evidence predicates. Include exact namespace/root/operation/plan digest and bounded file inventory. PREPARED/PUBLISHING partial histories may enter only the exact recovery inspection that existing recovery rules permit; no ordinary lease or backup borrow may pass. The other namespace and every non-own pending operation always deny. PUBLISHING with exact applied NewBytes may be inspected/completed; it cannot abort or replay ReplaceFile. Unknown/mixed/tampered backup/stage/hash evidence denies. C own inspection must similarly preserve its existing NOT_APPLIED/ABORTED rules. Revalidate under the held lock; no serialized permit, callback, bool or raw handle supplies authority.",
